{"role":"agent","utterance":"Hi Maya, this is Riley, a virtual recruiting assistant with Acme Health. I'm calling about the Medical ICU nurse position you applied for. Do you have a few minutes?"}
{"role":"user","utterance":"Yeah, I can talk now."}
{"role":"agent","utterance":"Thanks. This call is recorded and shared with our recruiting team. Is it okay to continue?"}
{"role":"user","utterance":"Yes, that's fine."}
{"role":"agent","utterance":"Do you currently hold an active Colorado RN license or a multistate RN license?"}
{"role":"user","utterance":"I have a Colorado license. Actually, you know what, I've changed my mind. I'd like to stop the screening here."}

{"role":"agent","utterance":"Before we get into your background, I want to let you know this call is recorded and shared with the Acme Health recruiting team. May we continue?"}
{"role":"user","utterance":"Sure, go ahead."}
{"role":"agent","utterance":"What RN license are you practicing under right now?"}
{"role":"user","utterance":"My Colorado RN license is active. And if you're about to ask about certs, my BLS and ACLS are both current. I renewed them together in September."}

{"role":"agent","utterance":"For my last screening question, tell me about a time you spoke up for a patient whose needs had been overlooked."}
{"role":"user","utterance":"A patient who was hard of hearing kept getting updates while people were facing the computer. I asked the team to face her when they spoke and made sure she could see the plan in writing. Before I left, she walked me through it in her own words."}
{"role":"agent","utterance":"You changed how the team gave updates and checked that the plan made sense to her. What questions do you have about the position?"}
{"role":"user","utterance":"No, I think we've covered everything I wanted to ask. Thanks for taking the time."}
